# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF, on every platform. Git's autocrlf would
# otherwise give a Windows clone CRLF line endings, and a CRLF shebang makes Linux
# fail the launcher with the cryptic "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M".
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell reads a BOM-less .ps1 as ANSI; CRLF is its native form on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
